      "sequence_position": 18,
      "problem": "Which of the following is the correct interpretation of $g:R\\to R?$\n\nI. The domain of $g$ is $R$\n\nII. The codomain of $g$ is $R$\n\nIII. The range of $g$ is $R$",
      "worked_solution": "The notation \n\n$$\ng:R\\to R\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $g$ maps the set $R$ to the set $R.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $R,$ and\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $R.$ Note that this is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
